<article class="env-lemma" id="0D33">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D33">Lemma <span data-tag="0D33">71.14.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $\mathcal{L}$ be an invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $Y' \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $f' : X' \to Y'$ be the base change of $f$ and denote $\mathcal{L}'$ the pullback of $\mathcal{L}$ to $X'$. If $\mathcal{L}$ is $f$-ample, then $\mathcal{L}'$ is $f'$-ample. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from the definition! (Hint: transitivity of base change.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>